A reinforcement learning project based on Stable-Baselines3 and Gymnasium for training and testing DQN agents in the CartPole environment.
Project Structure
RL1/
├── models/                 # Model storage directory
│   └── dqn_cartpole.zip   # Trained model file
├── train.py               # Training script
├── test.py                # Testing script
└── README.md             # Project documentation
Features
Training Script (train.py)
Trains a DQN agent on the CartPole-v1 environment
Trains for 1,000,000 steps with progress bar display
Automatically saves the trained model to a specified directory
Testing Script (test.py)
Loads and tests the trained model with visualization
Observes agent performance in a graphical interface
Runs for up to 5000 steps or until task failure
Requirements
Required Dependencies
pip install gymnasium
pip install stable-baselines3
Optional Dependencies (for rendering)
pip install pygame  # For graphical rendering
Usage
1. Train the Agent
python train.py
After training, the model will be saved to: C:\Users\21753\Desktop\RL1\models\dqn_cartpole.zip
2. Test the Agent
python test.py
Note: Ensure the model file exists before running the test script
Configuration
Path Configuration
Modify the following path in the code to match your system:
base_dir = "C:\\Users\\21753\\Desktop\\RL1"  # Change to your project path
Training Parameters
Algorithm: DQN
Training steps: 1,000,000
Environment: CartPole-v1
Policy network: MLP (Multi-Layer Perceptron)
Important Notes
Path Requirements: Ensure the project path exists and has write permissions
Model Dependency: The test script requires running the training script first to generate the model file
Rendering Support: Testing requires graphical interface support for visualization
Hardware Requirements: Training may take considerable time; GPU acceleration is recommended
Troubleshooting
Common Issues
Model file not found error: Run train.pyfirst to train the model
Rendering errors: Install pygame or check graphics drivers
Path errors: Modify base_dirto the correct project path
